00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:35.980
I do have a quick little aside about the Star Wars space plane.

00:23:36.740 --> 00:23:46.540
Yeah, go for it. So apparently there was very briefly in the late 80s, a competitor to NASA space shuttle.

00:23:46.820 --> 00:23:48.020
They call it the Buran.

00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:54.160
And it was basically just a ripoff of the space shuttle's design.

00:23:54.860 --> 00:23:58.300
And it never did a manned flight.

00:23:58.500 --> 00:24:02.400
It went into space for a few hours once without anybody in it.

00:24:02.400 --> 00:24:04.020
And then it was retired.

00:24:04.300 --> 00:24:05.820
And then the Soviet Union fell.

00:24:06.660 --> 00:24:11.980
So I just think it's funny because I thought that like, oh, why are they just putting the space shuttle as an enemy?

00:24:13.140 --> 00:24:20.600
And I didn't know until I played this game and looked up stuff about it that that was a real thing.

00:24:24.380 --> 00:24:28.640
They also improved the landing sequence, or so I'm told.

00:24:28.840 --> 00:24:31.560
The only thing I could really tell about it is that it's much shorter.

00:24:31.560 --> 00:24:33.800
So if you fail, you fail faster.

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:43.540
But I guess you could argue that the information of what you need to do to land is given to you more clearly than in Top Gun 1.

00:24:44.200 --> 00:24:45.840
Granted, it's still the same information.

00:24:45.840 --> 00:24:48.580
You still have to make sure you match the speed and the altitude.

00:24:48.840 --> 00:24:52.960
It's just that in Top Gun 1, it was just text being displayed.

00:24:52.960 --> 00:25:03.820
Whereas in Top Gun 2, there's a, you know, it's all conveyed on one screen telling you up, down, speed, 288.

00:25:03.820 --> 00:25:05.200
Yeah, your target speed.

00:25:06.120 --> 00:25:13.940
So this is basically taking a boss battle and turning it into a quick time event.

00:25:15.180 --> 00:25:18.920
In the first one, you kind of had to get a feel for landing.

00:25:18.920 --> 00:25:20.800
And I'm not saying that that's a good thing.

00:25:21.100 --> 00:25:28.980
Like, it's a pretty routine thing that they made unnecessarily hard and it took us a while to get the gist of it.

00:25:28.980 --> 00:25:36.220
But now it's just like, you follow the instructions on the screen and it feels like you're not landing.

00:25:36.220 --> 00:25:38.720
You're just saying, uh-huh, yeah, down.

00:25:39.160 --> 00:25:40.540
Yeah, slow.

00:25:41.160 --> 00:25:43.300
You're just doing what it says to do.

00:25:43.440 --> 00:25:46.100
So it feels like you aren't really learning anything.

00:25:46.100 --> 00:25:48.280
You're just copying.

00:25:48.840 --> 00:25:52.400
Like, my biggest takeaway from it is that it's just this, it's pretty much the same thing.

00:25:52.640 --> 00:25:56.840
It's just a lot more broad, a lot less touchy.

00:25:56.960 --> 00:25:58.660
You know, you don't have to be as exact.

00:25:58.940 --> 00:26:00.200
It's just like up, down, you know.

00:26:00.200 --> 00:26:09.000
I did replay a landing sequence from the original and, yeah, I mean, this isn't, uh, I don't think this is in any way, I think this is, if anything, supporting your argument, Sean.

00:26:09.280 --> 00:26:14.700
But, um, but I played the first one and it was a lot more, like, up, left, right, down.

00:26:14.820 --> 00:26:19.820
Like, I was, like, every second I had to be pressing a button to, like, just to really stay lined up that whole time.

00:26:19.820 --> 00:26:27.280
Whereas this, it was just kind of, like, I felt more like I was just kind of, like, in the background sort of managing the plane rather than flying it.

00:26:27.400 --> 00:26:40.720
I was also surprised that just how, you know, maybe this is what you guys are saying, but, like, how literally you have to tweak things to the point where even they were saying that you have to, like, straighten out with the carrier to land on it.

00:26:41.200 --> 00:26:42.940
I felt like even that was kind of forgiving.

00:26:42.940 --> 00:26:46.140
It's not like you need to be head-on with the runway to land.

00:26:46.140 --> 00:26:49.320
You just have to make sure you're lined up with the carrier at all.

00:26:49.320 --> 00:26:55.040
But the speed also isn't, like, dramatically different than what you start the landing sequence at.

00:26:55.100 --> 00:26:59.680
